stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Active: Admin: POST /api/v1/authorities\n(authority created, immediately active)

    Active --> Active: Admin updates authority\n(name, subsets changed)

    Active --> Deleted: Admin: DELETE /api/v1/authorities/{id}\n(authority removed)

    Deleted --> [*]: Authority removed from registry\nAuthority users lose access

    note right of Active
        State: Active
        - Authority users can search identifiers: GET /v1/identifiers/{id}
        - Authority users can request datasets: GET /v1/dataset/{gateId}/{platformId}/{datasetId}
        - Subsets field controls which eFTI subsets users may request
        - Per-user subsets must be a subset of authority.subsets
        - Authority users can send follow-ups: POST /v1/follow-up/...
    end note

    note right of Deleted
        State: Deleted
        - authorityRegistry lookup throws error
        - All authority users get 401 on next request
        - Historical data access logs retained (GDPR)
    end note
